 "notes": "Single map sheet read from OCR (page 1). Map symbols beside unit names are garbled ('QHiw |', 'Gan', 'art', 'Hoo', '701 tm', '[ tas |', 'Ti |') and were not recorded, except the cross-section-only unit (TEmu, from 'TEmy' and the section label; inferred, sent to review). The Water unit was not recorded. Legend-only features (contact, drill-hole symbol) were not recorded as values. Four thicknesses printed with '|' for a digit are read as 1, flagged inferred and sent to review. The Toney Bay Member description begins 'The Waccamaw formation is ...' as printed. The Low Falls beds description is a placeholder ('xxx').\nSUBSURFACE: cross section A-A' (page 1) is recorded with its vertical exaggeration and the three drill holes labelled on it (38-312, 38-299, 38-295; their logs are on file at the SCGS, not in this document); its elevation scale (160 to 40 feet, 48 to 12 meters), highway crossings and the unit label TEmu can't be tied to distances, so no units along it were recorded, and its datum is not printed. Uppermost elevations of the Toney Bay Member (95 ft) and Marietta unit (135 ft) and the 80-ft river-terrace elevation are not tied to a place and stay in unit descriptions. Datum: horizontal 1927 North American Datum; contour interval 5 feet on the 1979 base map (page 1).",
